 Deployment helpers for the internal services.
 
-`bin/notify-deploy.sh SERVICE VERSION` restarts the service on the deploy host and posts a
-message to the release channel. The webhook URL comes from `SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL` in the
-environment; per-service settings live in `etc/services.conf`.
+## notify-deploy.sh
+
+```
+bin/notify-deploy.sh [--dry-run] SERVICE VERSION [NOTE]
+```
+
+Restarts the service on the deploy host and posts a message to the release channel. The
+webhook URL comes from `SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL` in the environment; per-service settings live in
+`etc/services.conf`.
+
+- `NOTE` (optional third argument): a short release note, added on a new line below the
+  "Deployed ..." message in Slack. Up to 500 characters, no control characters (so no
+  newlines). Quote it so the shell passes it as one argument:
+  `bin/notify-deploy.sh web 1.4.2 "Fixes login timeout"`.
+- `--dry-run`: prints what the script would do (the remote command, the config in use, and the
+  Slack payload) and exits without restarting the service or posting. It never prints the
+  webhook URL, only whether it is set, and does not need `SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL` to be set.
+
+`SERVICE` must match `^[a-z][a-z0-9_-]{0,63}$` and `VERSION` must match
+`^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._+-]{0,63}$`; anything else is rejected with exit status 65.
+Usage errors exit 64.
